# Redirects — Netlify / Cloudflare Pages `_redirects` format.
#
# Purpose: resolve every URL the Webflow site served that this rebuild does not,
# so external links and search results land somewhere real instead of a 404.
# The migration plan's rule is that dead paths are resolved deliberately rather
# than left to rot.
#
# Format: <from> <to> <status>
# 301 = permanent. Use 301 so search engines transfer signal and update their index.

# ── Template residue from the purchased Webflow theme ────────────────────────
# These served Lorem Ipsum and fabricated articles to the public, linked from the
# primary navigation. They are not migrated. See build-context/DECISIONS.md.
/template-info/blog        /    301
/template-info/shop        /    301
/template-info/styleguide  /    301
/template-info/licensing   /    301
/template-info/changelog   /    301
/template-info/*           /    301

# ── /blog ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Returned 404 on the live site. The blog is built but shipped disabled, so this
# redirect stands in for it.
#
# ⚠️ WHEN THE BLOG IS ENABLED, DELETE THIS LINE. Netlify and Cloudflare both
# apply _redirects BEFORE serving a static file at the same path, so leaving it
# would shadow the real /blog index and the blog would appear not to work.
# This is called out in docs/enable-blog.md.
/blog                      /    301

# ── /gcx ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A dated event landing page ("GCX, Orlando, Aug 4-5") that was never in the site
# inventory. Dropped by direction. The URL is live today, so it redirects rather
# than 404s.
/gcx                       /    301

# ── Legacy / alternate paths ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
/work                      /projects   301
/about                     /team       301

# ── E-commerce scaffolding ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No such functionality has ever existed on this site; these are unremoved
# artifacts of the purchased template.
/checkout                  /    301
/paypal-checkout           /    301
/order-confirmation        /    301

# ── Extension-stripping ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The rebuilt site serves extensionless URLs. Anything that hardcoded a .html
# extension must still resolve. Retired CCPA / Notice at Collection URLs
# permanently redirect to the updated Privacy Policy (2026-08-12).
/index.html                /                        301
/privacy-policy.html       /privacy-policy          301
/ccpa.html                 /privacy-policy          301
/notice-at-collection.html /privacy-policy          301
/ccpa                      /privacy-policy          301
/notice-at-collection      /privacy-policy          301
/services.html             /services                301
/projects.html             /projects                301
/team.html                 /team                    301
/contact.html              /contact                 301
